* The passage between the volcano's east end and the potion room (openc2e
* Creatures 2 project, our own script; owner, 2026-11-13). Run by openc2e
* after the world loads (Additions folder); safe to repeat.
*
* The volcano's east ledge (room 167, walking line y 2189) and the potion
* room across the world's east-west seam (room 105, floor y 2329) were parted
* by a sealed rock pillar (room 213, x 8240-8352, every door shut). The short
* way round the world they are a step apart, so food trips, smells and the
* sociable pulled creatures into that wall from both sides for long spells
* (owner's screencast). Now a way leads through:
* - the pillar's room is the passage: its floor slopes from the ledge's
*   height down to the potion room's (the line of the ramp picture), and the
*   ledge's end and the potion room's first 80 px slope with it;
* - the passage opens into the potion room for good, and onto the ledge
*   through a door: the volcano's own hatch door (the southwest one, 2 9 10),
*   mirrored, its post on the wall line (x 8240); like that one it is pressed
*   to open or shut, and starts open;
* - pictures made on the player's machine from their own game by
*   tools/sprites/volcano_passage.py: the seam between the two rooms hidden
*   (zvps), the passage carved out of the rock by light (zvpc), the ramp
*   (zvpr) and the mirrored door (zvdr). They lie behind creatures and
*   objects, the door in front of them.

* the room map
* (the ramp starts where the ledge's lava slab stops, x 8205, and ends just
* short of the potion room's bookshelf arch, x 80: about 33 degrees at its
* steepest; at 40 degrees creatures could not walk up it)
ssfc 167 5 0 235 50 210 165 210 180 202 200 190
ssfc 213 8 0 190 16 181 32 170 48 160 64 150 80 139 96 128 112 118
ssfc 105 6 0 118 20 105 40 93 60 81 80 70 802 70
setv door 0 213 105 255

* the pictures (classifiers 2 3 250-252), the door (2 9 211)
enum 2 3 250 kill targ next
enum 2 3 251 kill targ next
enum 2 3 252 kill targ next
enum 2 9 211 kill targ next
inst new: simp zvps 1 0 2 0 setv cls2 2 3 250 setv attr 0 mvto 8272 1700 slow
inst new: simp zvpc 1 0 3 0 setv cls2 2 3 251 setv attr 0 mvto 8215 2010 slow
inst new: simp zvpr 1 0 4 0 setv cls2 2 3 252 setv attr 0 mvto 8205 2188 slow
inst new: simp zvdr 5 0 6 0 setv cls2 2 9 211 setv attr 4 setv ov00 0 pose 4 mvto 8055 2028 slow
setv door 0 167 213 255

* the door: frame 0 shut (seen edge-on), 4 open; as the southwest door's own
* script, with the passage's rooms. Creatures pull it as often as they push
* it (activate 2), and the game's doors answer only a push, so a pull did
* nothing (owner, 2026-11-13: "seems like no one can open this door"; a
* norn pulled it over and over). Both doors now open or shut to a pull too:
* this one (2 9 211) and the southwest door (2 9 10, its own push script
* copied: it opens between rooms 212 and 163).
* (owner, 2026-11-14: a crowd at this exit, "creatures going against each
* other in attempting to push and pull the door"). With a press opening or
* shutting it, in a crowd each press undid the last: 6.4% of all the
* world's choices were made here, by 109 creatures at mean Hunger 205,
* about 1,400 of them pushes, pulls and "deactivates" of the door, most as
* steps on a route through it. Now a push or pull only opens a door, and
* "deactivate" does nothing; the doors start open. The same for the
* volcano's southwest hatch door (2 9 10), the other door creatures worked
* over and over. (A first version also shut each door by itself when nobody
* was within 120 px: in three matched copies against three with the old
* scripts, the crowd at the passage halved, 3.0-4.8% of all choices to
* 1.9-2.1%, but the southwest door grew busier, 0.9-1.9% to 1.5-2.8%, as
* each arrival found it shut and opened it again; so neither shuts now.)
scrp 2 9 211 1
  doif ov00 eq 1
    anim [01234] over snde dor1 setv ov00 0 setv door 0 167 213 255
  endi
  setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 9 211 2
  doif ov00 eq 1
    anim [01234] over snde dor1 setv ov00 0 setv door 0 167 213 255
  endi
  setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 9 211 0
  setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 9 10 1
  doif ov00 eq 1
    anim [01234] over snde dor1 setv ov00 0 setv door 1 212 163 255
  endi
  setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 9 10 2
  doif ov00 eq 1
    anim [01234] over snde dor1 setv ov00 0 setv door 1 212 163 255
  endi
  setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 9 10 0
  setv actv 0
endm
* both doors open at load (the southwest one is kept with the world, and
* may have been saved shut), with no timer
enum 2 9 211 setv rnge 120 tick 0 next
enum 2 9 10 setv rnge 120 tick 0 doif ov00 eq 1 pose 4 setv ov00 0 setv door 1 212 163 255 endi next
